  "fanTake": "Twenty to three. At home. Against Pittsburgh. Look, I'm not going to pretend this was vintage Patriots football — our offense was actually below average by EPA, and we converted just a third of our third downs — but sometimes a win is a win, especially when your defense is playing the kind of suffocating football that holds an opponent to a field goal. Rhamondre Stevenson was our best player by win probability added, which tells you we leaned on the run game and didn't need to do much fancy. The Steelers managed zero touchdowns on their one red-zone trip, and converted just 17% of their third downs. We're not lighting the world on fire, but we're getting wins at home, and right now that'll do.",
